{"type":"text","timestamp":1784514280651,"sessionID":"ses_082ae2e3bffenPcx9bgPSZp5kY","part":{"id":"prt_f7d56d19100152DUC077WROGf6","messageID":"msg_f7d569387001LOEuNXf8T9qcCm","sessionID":"ses_082ae2e3bffenPcx9bgPSZp5kY","type":"text","text":"Results confirmed. Here's the summary:\n\n**Annual average consumption of the customer with the lowest consumption in each segment (CZK, 2013):**\n\n| Segment | Min Consumption | # Customers at Min | Annual Average |\n|---------|----------------|-------------------|----------------|\n| KAM | -6044.38 | 1 | -6044.38 |\n| LAM | 2.24 | 1 | 2.24 |\n| SME | -14007.10 | 1 | -14007.10 |\n\n**Differences:**\n- SME − LAM = **-14009.34**\n- LAM − KAM = **6046.62**\n- KAM − SME = **7962.72**\n\nEach segment has exactly one customer with the minimum total 2013 consumption, so the annual average equals that customer's total consumption.\n\n---\n\nFinal Answer: The differences in annual average consumption are: SME − LAM = -14009.34, LAM − KAM = 6046.62, KAM − SME = 7962.72\nEvidence SQL: \n```sql\nWITH customer_totals AS (\n  SELECT c.CustomerID, c.Segment, SUM(y.Consumption) as total_consumption\n  FROM customers c\n  JOIN yearmonth y ON c.CustomerID = y.CustomerID\n  WHERE c.Currency = 'CZK'\n    AND y.Date BETWEEN '201301' AND '201312'\n  GROUP BY c.CustomerID, c.Segment\n),\nmin_per_segment AS (\n  SELECT Segment, MIN(total_consumption) as min_consumption\n  FROM customer_totals\n  GROUP BY Segment\n),\navg_per_segment AS (\n  SELECT m.Segment, \n         ROUND(SUM(ct.total_consumption) / COUNT(*), 2) as annual_average\n  FROM min_per_segment m\n  JOIN customer_totals ct ON m.Segment = ct.Segment AND ct.total_consumption = m.min_consumption\n  GROUP BY m.Segment\n)\nSELECT \n  ROUND(MAX(CASE WHEN Segment = 'SME' THEN annual_average END) - MAX(CASE WHEN Segment = 'LAM' THEN annual_average END), 2) as diff_SME_LAM,\n  ROUND(MAX(CASE WHEN Segment = 'LAM' THEN annual_average END) - MAX(CASE WHEN Segment = 'KAM' THEN annual_average END), 2) as diff_LAM_KAM,\n  ROUND(MAX(CASE WHEN Segment = 'KAM' THEN annual_average END) - MAX(CASE WHEN Segment = 'SME' THEN annual_average END), 2) as diff_KAM_SME\nFROM avg_per_segment\n```","time":{"start":1784514269585,"end":1784514280647}}}
